WEBVTT

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:09.010
Saiki, are you used to Japanese yet?

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:12.090
No, not so much.
I make many mistakes when speaking.

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:13.510
Well, learn already.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:15.350
Right now, I can't count on you
to do my grocery shopping.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:17.260
Yes, I will do my best, Kissaki.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.060
You better.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.020
Are you kind of soft on Saiki?

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.990
Please give it back, Miyakoshi.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:00.240
I'LL TRY GETTING REVENGE

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:59.320
Your wish didn't come true,
so the monetary offering...

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:01.080
8,764 yen.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.080
Plus 1,000 yen.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:03.870
Gimme a discount!

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:05.790
That's not the way
you ask someone to do something.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:06.830
Give me a discount!

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:08.290
You're doing it wrong, Higashida!

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:11.670
The basic rule of collecting a debt
is not going soft on the debtor.

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:13.800
In fact, you should increase the amount.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:14.840
Increase it?

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:15.880
- Higashida!
- Higashida!

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:17.470
Higashida, wake up!

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:18.720
Don't be a debt collector!

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.100
N-No, I wasn't really...

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:21.550
She told me,

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:24.350
"I gave you a present, so your
return gift has to be three times that."

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:26.140
- So she tripled my debt!
- Shindou...

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:28.940
Even though she gave me
dog food! It's crazy!

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:30.940
Shindou, Kamakura is listening.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:33.940
She's an ogre! An ogre!

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:37.240
I understand,
so please stop hurting yourself.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.070
Fine, 8,000 yen.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:41.450
9,000 yen.

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:44.990
Give it up, Miyakoshi.

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:48.370
You need to take responsibility
for what you made.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:50.250
You're the one who made that chocolate.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:53.210
You're the one
who made that Higashida, too.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:57.920
- Give me a discount, at least by 1,000 yen!
- 9,000 yen.

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:57.920
Pay me back, too.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.890
But you never gave me anything.

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:03.220
Cash is fine. Pay me back triple.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:05.430
We're talking about zero,
so three times that is still...

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.810
You didn't know?

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:08.940
Three times zero is 30,000.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:10.520
Is that right?

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:11.900
Manager...

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.820
Kisaki, it's not right
to sponge off of the manager.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:16.650
After all, he's got money.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:18.070
After all?

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:19.820
Why do you have so much money?

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:24.580
I'm surrounded by weirdos here,
so you didn't really stand out until now.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:27.120
But when I think carefully,
it doesn't make sense.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.870
After all Miyakoshi's violence,
you haven't died.

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:30.830
That's rude!

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:34.340
And Kisaki extorts you for large sums
of money, which you just keep paying.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:35.050
That's rude.

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:37.460
And you're incompetent,
but you're the manager for some reason.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.550
INCOMPETENT

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:39.920
Senpai!

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:41.890
Tasaka.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.800
TASAKA

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:44.800
Milady! Is Milady here?!

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.020
She was a little while ago, but...

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:49.810
Where did you go, Milady?!

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:50.770
This is Tasaka, Kamakura's bodyguard.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.150
To be precise, I'm a bodyguard
who watches over Mr. Shindou

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.360
to make sure Milady doesn't kill him.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:59.990
But a second ago,
you called the manager senpai.

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:02.740
Yes, he was my senpai
back in high school.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:06.910
He was so strong
and often helped me out.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.370
- No way.
- No way.

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:09.370
A knee-jerk denial?!

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:11.870
Tasaka always tells huge whoppers.

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:12.870
Even you?!

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:16.420
There's no way a useless adult
who just likes cute things could be like that.

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:18.000
U-Useless adult...

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:22.300
W-Well, anyway, he was
a bad-ass juvenile delinquent!

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:24.510
Honestly, he was so tough!

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:25.180
Who?!

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:28.350
That is kind of like the manager!

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:29.350
I know, right?!

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:32.770
He wouldn't talk,
but the cat on his head would meow,

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:34.850
so it was said the guys he'd beat
in a fight would have nightmares

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:36.940
for three days and nights about that cat.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:38.400
So the nickname that stuck was

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:40.360
Cat Sakaki!

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:41.820
Kisaki?!

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:43.780
True...

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:47.620
My cat, Miyo, refused to get off my head.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:52.000
Everyone avoided me,
but I wouldn't call that being bullied.

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:55.920
But weren't you always fighting back then?

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:59.300
No, the leader of the juvenile delinquents
back then was my friend,

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:00.920
but he was so weak...

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:04.550
<i>Fight in my place
to give our school some dignity!</i>

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:06.590
<i>I'm not into fighting.</i>

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:09.220
<i>I'll buy the best brand
of cat food for Miyoko!</i>

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:12.600
<i>Miyo stood up!</i>

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:14.980
So it couldn't be helped.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.730
<i>You're the one who can't be helped.</i>

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:20.690
After high school graduation,
Miyo stopped riding my head,

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:23.190
but then scary people came to scout me.

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:24.570
I went along, too!

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:28.030
<i>Why Kamakura's?!
I thought I'd at least think that.</i>

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:30.620
I didn't think that would be a good idea,

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:32.870
so I've been turning
them down all this time.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:35.500
But they told me to take
this money as a promise...

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:38.130
that I wouldn't join anywhere else.

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:40.050
There was nothing I could do.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:41.840
<i>There really is nothing you can do.</i>

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.340
Now do you see how great he is?!

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:45.510
No, just the opposite.

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:49.470
Then why is a manager like that
an easy victory for Miyakoshi

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:52.140
and easy pickings for
the money-grubbing Kisaki?

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:56.020
The weirdness level of this place
is going to skyrocket!

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:57.900
I refuse to accept that state of things!

00:05:57.900 --> 00:05:59.690
Manager, you need to be normal!

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:01.780
<i>Does he hate me?</i>

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:03.650
But... Oh, I forgot!

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:05.860
Milady! Or rather, Mr. Shindou!

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:07.860
Excuse me! Pardon me!

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:12.580
So how did a loser like you
end up being the manager here?

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:16.210
Um, it's complicated.

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:17.080
Wanna hear?

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.420
Nah, I think I've heard enough for one day.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:23.380
Muranushi.

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:26.800
If there's something you'd like as thanks
for the cookies you gave me last time...

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:28.550
No, that's okay.

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:29.890
Well, I can't just give you nothing.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:33.350
Then do me a favor. Go out with me.

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:37.100
U-Um... Go where?

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:39.440
An art supply store.

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:42.070
I need supplies to use for class,
but they're heavy to carry.

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:44.730
I won't interject! I will not interject!

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:45.780
Excuse me!

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:47.030
Saiki!

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:48.660
This, too, please.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:50.160
Roger.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:52.950
Come to think of it, Saiki,
do you remember my name?

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:54.160
U-Um...

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:56.450
Um... Adachi.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:58.040
Correct.

00:06:58.040 --> 00:06:59.040
Kouno.

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:00.040
Bingo!

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:02.460
Malignantushi.

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:05.380
Give that man a cigar.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:06.380
Lucky!

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:11.140
That's no good.

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:13.600
You need to think about the words
before you use them,

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:14.640
Adachi.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:18.770
If you get cocky,
you're going to get hurt, Adachi.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:23.480
Oh, no. I mixed up Saiki and Adachi.

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:24.900
Sorry, Adachi.

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:29.280
All joking aside, it makes me sad
that you can't remember my name.

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:31.820
And since I'm sad, maybe I'll smile—

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:33.070
Don't smile!

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:37.500
You've got it wrong. I don't mean
smile at you, Adachi, but at Saiki.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:37.500
That's even worse!

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:40.540
You mean I should only smile
in front of you, Adachi?

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:43.540
Saiki, that's Sayuri Muranushi.

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:46.630
U-Usury Muranushi?

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:50.430
Kamakura.

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:52.890
Oh, Muranushi.
Is something the matter?

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:55.260
Did it go okay with the customer at table 5?

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:56.970
He picked a quarrel with me before,

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:58.680
so I avoided him
without even thinking about it.

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.690
Oh. He kind of tried to pick me up,

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:04.810
so I went boom with a roll of banknotes,
and then the black suit went boom,

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:06.400
and then all kinds of things went boom.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:07.400
Boom.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:11.740
Shiho is so kind to take pity on a scoundrel.

00:08:13.490 --> 00:08:15.620
After all, if Papa found out about it,

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.290
his chance in society would go boom.

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:18.120
Boom.

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:19.620
What's wrong?

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:24.170
If I were cuter, the customer
wouldn't have gone "boom."

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:27.380
I think you're cute, Muranushi.

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:28.460
Your eyelashes are like boom!

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:31.840
That's not true.
I can't even smile decently.

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:33.300
Oh, Muranushi.

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:36.010
You don't need to sell your smile
to the customers so cheaply!

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:39.890
I don't know what's going on,
but you work with customers!

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:41.690
Sheesh!

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:44.480
When you work in this industry,
you better be amiable!

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:46.730
At a family restaurant,
smiling is number one!

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:47.730
Right, Higashida?!

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:48.820
Yeah...

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:53.320
But for some reason, I have the feeling
that I'm not good at smiling lately.

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:54.320
Why?!

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:55.660
It's your fault.

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:59.660
Dammit! What the hell's wrong
with all of 'em?!

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:02.870
Kisaki, smile!

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:04.460
- Forget it.
- What?

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:07.380
You can't work in the service industry
if you're not a pro at smiling!

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:10.210
I see. Since I'm a pro, I guess I'd better.

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:12.970
Okay, that'll be 10,000 yen per smile.

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:14.430
Sakaki will pay!

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:19.100
Come to think of it,
at this restaurant, me aside,

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:21.060
neither Muranushi nor Kisaki smile.

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.230
Kamakura smiles,
but her behavior is questionable.

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:24.560
Shindou cries.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:26.350
Saiki doesn't understand the language.

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:28.310
The two in the kitchen
would be useless on the floor.

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:30.150
Sakaki would be even more useless.

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:31.690
Higashida has been acting weird lately.

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:33.490
I haven't seen a single smile out of him.

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:35.240
What's with this family restaurant?!

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:38.070
That's what I've been asking myself
since the day I started here.

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:42.830
Look, Yuuta!
I bought it with my allowance!

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:45.040
Y-You'll be arrested!

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:46.080
It's okay, it's okay!

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:48.790
K-Kamakura!

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:50.000
Huh? What is it?

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:52.880
S-Saiki! Be careful
about making a slip of the tongue!

00:09:53.670 --> 00:09:56.680
Please don't bully Shindou
just because he rejected you!

00:09:57.930 --> 00:09:59.550
<i>You should've made
a slip of the tongue there.</i>

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:03.140
Shiho, don't! He'll die!

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:04.140
You didn't mean it, right, Saiki?

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:05.810
It was one of your
usual misstatements, right?!

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:06.940
I made a mistake!

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:07.600
See?

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:10.860
Please don't be bad-tempered
just because Shindou ridiculed you!

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:12.230
Saiki, run!

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:13.230
Run away!

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:14.570
R-Right!

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:17.200
Shiho, that was just a verbal slip-up!

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:19.120
I didn't ridicule you,
you're not bad-tempered,

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:21.030
and just for argument's sake,
you don't bully me!

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:21.030
Move!

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:22.040
Shiho!

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:26.500
He didn't reject me!

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:27.500
That bothers you?!

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:30.040
Shiho... Shiho...

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:30.840
Kamakura...

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:33.340
You look like an angel right now.

00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:36.260
MEANT TO SAY "SWORDSWOMAN"

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:38.590
Please be more honest with your feelings.

00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:40.260
H-He's coming on to her?!

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:42.470
Are you okay?!

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:45.100
I'll let you off the hook for now.

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:46.640
But...

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:49.730
this is the second time in my life
that someone's made a fool of me!

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:50.690
Remember that...

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:52.690
Yuuta!

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:53.360
Me?!

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:55.900
<i>A comrade.</i>

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:58.820
Good job.

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:02.580
Jeez, Saiki! Come on!

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:05.450
You were so close to getting carved up!

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:07.120
That woman has no mercy!

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:12.130
Still, it was the first time
I saw Shiho like that! I was moved!

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:14.000
That's what she gets!

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.880
Hahaha, I say!

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:19.800
Now we know it's safe for him
to make as many mistakes as he likes!

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:22.720
But the other person's feelings get hurt.

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:26.930
Adachi, you're so kind to everyone.

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:30.310
You know, we're the ones
getting dragged into this.

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:35.070
Saiki, start with the syllabary.

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:38.070
Starve with the silly berry?

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:54.040
<i>Um, Higashida...</i>

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:55.500
<i>Nagata.</i>

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:57.550
<i>Um, actually...</i>

00:11:58.340 --> 00:11:59.340
<i>Is something up?</i>

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:00.590
<i>It's kind of late to mention this,</i>

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:02.720
<i>but Yanagiba is a little eccentric, isn't she?</i>

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:04.970
<i>Oh, yeah. Maybe.</i>

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:07.270
<i>She does always wear a scarf.</i>

00:12:07.270 --> 00:12:08.730
<i>But that's only because
she's sensitive to cold...</i>

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:12.230
<i>Yes, the scarf is fine, but um...</i>

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:16.780
<i>Oh, never mind.</i>

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:17.780
<i>See you!</i>

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:20.990
<i>Don't tell me Yanagiba is so quirky</i>

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:23.410
<i>that Nagata can't be friends with her.</i>

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:24.160
<i>Wait...</i>

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:27.120
It's hot.

00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:30.290
Ya-na-gi-ba!

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:34.460
Higashi, the heat's up too high.

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:36.460
You're sensitive to cold, aren't you?

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:38.670
Air conditioning is too cold in the summer.

00:12:38.670 --> 00:12:43.470
I think Japanese rely too much
on heating and air conditioning.

00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:45.470
It's connected to global warming

00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:47.850
and above all, is contrary to
co-existing with nature.

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:51.390
I'm saying we should value
the sense of the seasons more.

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:53.600
That's exactly what I'd like to tell you.

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:55.980
And yet, all you've got on is that scarf.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:58.230
What are you talking about?

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:01.190
If you don't wear a scarf in the winter,
you'll get a cold, right?

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:03.320
Yes, that's right. Of course.

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:05.700
If you don't wear a scarf in the winter,
your body will get cold,

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:08.370
which will then turn into a cold. Yeah.

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:10.830
Higashi, you have no common sense.

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:13.920
All right, Yanagiba.
I'm gonna clobber you!

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:17.840
Welcome.

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:21.970
Uh, um, thank you for always
looking after my daughter.

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:22.760
I...

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:25.090
Oh, not him? I'm sorry.

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:27.760
Pardon me. Um, I'm...

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:29.560
Muranushi's mother, I presume?

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:31.020
Mom.

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:32.230
Sayuri.

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:35.850
I'm going out, so here's the key.

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:39.110
Satoru is at home, but I locked the door.
You know how dangerous it is.

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:40.650
Going out? Don't tell me...

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:44.450
That's right. I suddenly got a call
for an exorcism job.

00:13:44.450 --> 00:13:46.490
Mom, quit joking.

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:47.820
I'm not joking.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:51.200
In a way, it seems like it'd be easier
to communicate with the mother.

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:52.950
If you're done here, then you can go.

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.580
I've got time, so get me a cup of coffee.

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:59.090
Sheesh. How can you be so easygoing?

00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:01.050
Dad hasn't even come home yet.

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:05.300
Your father is in the middle of a slightly
difficult exorcism, but he'll be home soon.

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:08.640
And Satoru is sick in bed
with a fever of unknown cause...

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:10.810
A weird spirit has taken
a liking to him, that's all.

00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:12.270
It'll clear up naturally, sooner or later.

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:15.020
Mom, cut it out.

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:16.600
You cut it out, Sayuri.

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:18.270
I'm going to work.

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:21.780
Um... Here.

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:28.820
Um, thank you for always
looking after my daughter, Adachi.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:30.410
I'm Sayuri's mother.

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:34.910
Mother?! I mean, you know my name?!

00:14:34.910 --> 00:14:37.330
Oh, well, I just saw your name tag.

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:38.710
Oh, my name tag...

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:41.000
I'm not wearing a name tag!

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:42.210
So it seems.

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:43.880
Even so,

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:46.970
this is an eccentric restaurant,
just like the rumors say.

00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:49.760
Irrespective of Sayuri's presence,
it's full of ghosts.

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:50.600
Is it?

00:14:50.930 --> 00:14:54.770
Even on the human side, there's a girl
possessed by an extremely seasonable spirit,

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:58.190
a boy who straddles the line
between life and death,

00:14:58.190 --> 00:15:00.520
and you, Adachi, possessed by Sayuri.

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:02.110
<i>How much does she know?</i>

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:04.570
Not that I would know
about such things...

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:05.740
<i>Is she reading my mind?!</i>

00:15:05.740 --> 00:15:08.820
Adachi, it seems you've seen
my daughter smile.

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:10.910
Although she hasn't said anything to me.

00:15:11.780 --> 00:15:13.160
I remember.

00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:14.740
When Sayuri was in elementary school,

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:17.120
she smiled at a classmate, Saitou.

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:20.540
He was a rascal before but became
a mere shadow of his former self,

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:22.790
acted suspiciously, and then...

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:25.510
This coffee is surprisingly good.

00:15:25.510 --> 00:15:26.510
I know, right?

00:15:26.510 --> 00:15:27.510
<i>What about Saitou?!</i>

00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:30.510
Well, Saitou is... alive.

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:32.140
Barely. Doing well...

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:34.850
<i>You just muttered "barely"!</i>

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:41.690
So I apologize for any trouble
my daughter has caused you.

00:15:41.690 --> 00:15:42.560
What?!

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:45.320
Not that it makes
a bit of difference what I say.

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:47.440
Please look up, Mrs. Muranushi.

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:49.070
She hasn't caused me any trouble.

00:15:49.070 --> 00:15:50.910
You're very kind, Adachi.

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:54.160
No, um, she really
hasn't given me any trouble.

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:57.870
Um, your daughter's smile is just
so beautiful that every time I recall it,

00:15:57.870 --> 00:16:01.540
I feel a pain in my chest
and the blood drains out of my face.

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:03.750
Wait, is that right?!

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:06.000
No! I mean, yes, but...

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.090
She hasn't done anything wrong!

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:08.840
Calm down, Adachi.

00:16:09.470 --> 00:16:13.350
Just knowing that my daughter
hasn't been a burden to you...

00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:15.470
Yes, of course! Sorry!

00:16:15.850 --> 00:16:19.060
It's fine. I'm relieved.

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:21.270
You just said it's fine, right?

00:16:21.270 --> 00:16:22.940
I'd better get going.

00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:24.900
- Um...
- Oh, that's right.

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:28.360
I'll give you these, Adachi, just in case.

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:31.910
Well, there you have it.

00:16:34.030 --> 00:16:36.330
I'm sorry, Adachi.

00:16:36.330 --> 00:16:38.750
My mother is kind of an airhead
in a weird way.

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:41.040
What did she give you?

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:42.580
I'll give it back to her.

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:47.300
Adachi, what did you
talk to my mother about?

00:16:47.300 --> 00:16:48.590
N-Nothing special.

00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:54.680
"Adachi, I don't want to trouble you, but..."

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.510
"It's no trouble at all.

00:16:56.510 --> 00:17:00.020
You're just so beautiful
that I feel a pain in my chest."

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:01.980
Did you fall in love
at first sight with my mother?

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:03.440
Not your mother!

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:05.900
NEXT DAY

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:08.480
Then this will happen...

00:17:08.980 --> 00:17:11.440
Exactly! You're surprisingly clever, Miri.

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:13.530
- Hello.
- Hi!

00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:16.200
Yanagiba, what are you doing here?

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:17.370
Nothing much.

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:20.040
Just charting this restaurant's
romantic relationships.

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:20.870
Romantic?!

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:24.710
I was curious, so I thought
I'd go over the situation.

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:26.040
I'm trying to be careful, too.

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:27.670
<i>She's trying to be careful!</i>

00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:30.670
B-But that's not so good, is it?

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:32.130
Around Higashi, too.

00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:35.390
Naga, calm down.

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:38.810
That being said, I don't really
know about that kind of stuff.

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:40.970
So can I just come up
with stuff that sounds interesting?

00:17:42.230 --> 00:17:43.640
I guess that would be okay.

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:44.640
Really?!

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:47.560
All right!
First, Kisaki is lying about her age...

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:49.020
Ow!

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:51.070
Don't get a laugh
at somebody else's expense.

00:17:51.690 --> 00:17:53.450
You're harsh.

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:56.660
Um, she's going out with the manager.

00:17:56.660 --> 00:17:58.320
I've had it with older guys already.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:01.790
Well, you'd better be careful,
too, little girls.

00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:02.700
Warning us about what?!

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:06.500
Senior in life, please just tell me
who's close to each other

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:08.460
in this restaurant,
between the men and women.

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:10.590
What would you do
with that information?

00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:11.590
Be careful.

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:13.590
Well, let's see...

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:16.430
Adachi and Muranushi,
Kamakura and Shindou,

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:17.930
maybe Higashida and Miyakoshi?

00:18:17.930 --> 00:18:19.430
The nearest people...

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:21.390
What about you, Kouno?

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:22.100
Left over.

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:23.560
Why do you have to put it like that?!

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:27.020
So aside from the one leftover,
everyone is dating each other?

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:29.610
Can I draw red lines
connecting the people?

00:18:29.610 --> 00:18:33.320
It's not so much dating
as the guys are possessed.

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:35.240
It seems like they're gonna die soon.

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:37.660
Especially Adachi and Shindou...

00:18:38.780 --> 00:18:41.410
So don't feel bad
about being a leftover, Kouno.

00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:43.120
What do you have against me?!

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:47.620
I feel sorry for Kouno,
so I'll draw a red line connecting us.

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:49.380
Dammit! Thank you!

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:53.510
U-Um... Higashida isn't possessed?

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:56.380
His mode of life is enshrouded in mystery.

00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:57.840
Not even I know.

00:18:57.840 --> 00:18:58.840
Ask the implementer.

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:01.510
Everybody, get to work!

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:05.600
I'm not actually in charge of Higashida.

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:07.520
Are you in love with him?

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:08.520
Not at all.

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:10.940
But you give chocolate
to the person you really like.

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:13.940
I wouldn't give dangerous materials
like that to someone I love.

00:19:15.650 --> 00:19:18.200
After all, we're talking about Higashida.

00:19:18.820 --> 00:19:21.740
The Higashida who has no social graces,
who's quick to criticize,

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:23.830
who acts so superior,
just because he's kind of smart.

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:26.790
I can't understand anybody
who would fall for that guy.

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:27.870
You're right.

00:19:27.870 --> 00:19:28.870
Naga...

00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:33.000
If there was anyone in love with Higashida,
I couldn't understand them.

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:36.210
Y-You've got it wrong!

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:40.010
It means something
when you fall in love with someone!

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:40.720
Not really.

00:19:41.090 --> 00:19:44.600
Sure, you're right
about Higashida, Miyakoshi.

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:46.770
His face is as expressionless
as a Noh mask,

00:19:46.770 --> 00:19:48.940
and he acts and talks like a cyborg,

00:19:48.940 --> 00:19:51.020
and I don't know
what happened to his looks...

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:52.440
I didn't say that.

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:54.570
But once you've decided
that you love someone,

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:57.110
you have a responsibility
to carry it through to the end!

00:19:57.110 --> 00:19:59.320
Love has no inherent responsibility.

00:20:00.570 --> 00:20:02.870
<i>She liked Higashida out of responsibility?</i>

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:05.290
A-Anyway, you shouldn't give chocolate

00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:07.370
to someone you don't
really like, Miyakoshi.

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:08.870
<i>And there's that.</i>

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:09.750
U-Um...

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:12.250
You have to take more responsibility
for your own actions!

00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:15.300
If you're going to give it to him,
fall in love first!

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:16.550
Wait, no!

00:20:16.550 --> 00:20:17.420
Is that okay?!

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:20.180
Calm down a little, Naga.

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:23.680
Yanagiba, I don't even know
what I'm saying.

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:26.430
I'm sure Hana-hana
doesn't understand either.

00:20:26.430 --> 00:20:29.640
No, I feel great remorse.

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:30.850
Miyakoshi—

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:34.150
I made Higashida eat that chocolate,
even though he hadn't done anything wrong,

00:20:34.150 --> 00:20:37.280
and then talked disparagingly
of him after he changed.

00:20:37.280 --> 00:20:40.610
I-I'll take responsibility...

00:20:41.070 --> 00:20:43.990
and make Higashida eat my cooking
until he turns back to normal!

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:46.490
See?

00:20:46.490 --> 00:20:48.120
All right!

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:51.000
Please tell me how to make chocolate!

00:20:52.330 --> 00:20:56.090
<i>There's no way I can deal
with that murderous chocolate.</i>

00:20:56.630 --> 00:20:59.960
<i>I mean, in the first place,
are we romantic rivals?</i>

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:02.050
<i>In that case, I should
show humanity, even to my enemy...</i>

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:06.050
<i>But at this rate, Higashida will face
death again and it'll be half my fault.</i>

00:21:06.550 --> 00:21:08.260
You'd better take responsibility.

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:12.810
If you don't mind my help...

00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:16.020
Yes! Thank you very much!

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:18.480
It's tough to be young.

00:21:19.110 --> 00:21:20.990
Wait for me, Higashida!

00:21:24.740 --> 00:21:26.410
Do I have a cold?

00:21:27.740 --> 00:21:29.080
Muranushi's mother...

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:33.000
Didn't she say something
about performing an exorcism?

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:35.000
That does sound like shady work,

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.500
so I guess it's no wonder
Muranushi is repelled by it.

00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:41.300
It was nice meeting you the other day.

00:21:42.130 --> 00:21:46.220
A girl near you
means to make you a victim.

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:48.810
Exorcising her will take
considerable effort and sacrifice.

00:21:48.810 --> 00:21:51.730
And if you don't exorcise her,
the world will probably be destroyed.

00:21:51.730 --> 00:21:53.060
Proceed with caution.

00:21:54.890 --> 00:21:56.020
<i>She's the real deal.</i>

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:36.040
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

00:23:26.360 --> 00:23:29.410
There you have it. Time sure does fly,
as it's chocolate season again.

00:23:29.410 --> 00:23:32.660
<i>Generally speaking, chocolate is delicious!
Hey, long hair, give me some chocolate!</i>

00:23:31.030 --> 00:23:33.200
This is an eating establishment,
so you're not allowed inside.

00:23:33.080 --> 00:23:36.040
FATE SURVIVAL

00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:34.330
<i>Foiled!</i>

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:36.040
Next time, "Fate Survival."
